      {
        "id": 77332,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-21T17:10:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So would you shuffle both his picture card  and  his text card into the deck, or just one of them (and put the other card to one side for the time being)?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Very good question, since they are both character cards, but only one is a target, and that is the one being destroyed.</p>\n<p>I would wager only the picture card gets shuffled in.</p>\n<p>The question is what happens if he gets played. &nbsp;It isn't the \"Start of the game\" so none of that text would apply, I would guess he would go on the side the text card was on, and you would just have to knock his HP down again.</p>",
