        "name": "danmarshall14",
        "username": "danmarshall14",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/danmarshall14/{size}/1944_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-22T18:17:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Nielzabub\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nielzabub/48/1986_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Nielzabub:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If the Chairman is indestructible, that means if you take him down before the Operative, his text is still active giving all of his thugs and operatives bonuses. You would need to add another line specifying that his text is blank or something like that.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's exactly how we played it the other night. &nbsp;We had no idea what to do with him since the Operative was still alive, so we just said he's reduced to 0 HP and remains in play (along with all his effects). &nbsp;The card that heals the Chairman and the Operative happened to come up as well, so we had to heal her by 6 and heal the Chairman from 0 HP to 6 HP (again, because we were unsure what else to do).<br><br>It actually made the game pretty challenging; I liked it.</p>",
